### Bassign API — field sync smoke test (open in Visual Studio and click "Send request")
@api = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Sign in as a staff member (dev seed) — copy accessToken into @token below
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "tendai@bassign.local", "password": "Staff!2345" }

###
@token = paste-access-token-here

### 2. Full pull (since=0): Tendai's open tasks + the sync token
GET {{api}}/sync/tasks?since=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Push an accept twice with the SAME opId → "applied" then "duplicate" (idempotent)
#    Put one of Tendai's task ids in taskId (assign one to him on the web first).
POST {{api}}/sync/push
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "operations": [ { "opId": "6f1c2a1e-1111-4a5b-9c3d-000000000001", "taskId": "put-task-id-here", "action": "accept" } ] }

### --- WhatsApp (step 12b) ---
@waToken = dev-webhook-token-change-me

### Link status for the signed-in user
GET {{api}}/me/whatsapp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Start linking — returns a 6-digit code; send "LINK <code>" from the phone (or the simulator)
POST {{api}}/me/whatsapp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Webhook: wrong token → 404
POST {{api}}/webhooks/whatsapp/wrong-token
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Webhook: a text message from an unknown number → enrollment reply (see /dev/whatsapp in the Web app)
POST {{api}}/webhooks/whatsapp/{{waToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"object":"whatsapp_business_account","entry":[{"id":"x","changes":[{"field":"messages","value":{"messaging_product":"whatsapp","messages":[{"from":"263779999999","id":"wamid.HTTPTEST1","timestamp":"1764000000","type":"text","text":{"body":"hi"}}]}}]}]}
